course: dictionary
lesson: 13431
title: Homogenised: made all the same
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Homogenised is one of these words. «The milk in the carton is homogenised, so the cream does not rise to the top.» The clue is the cream staying mixed in, so homogenised means mixed evenly all the way through.
explain: Homogenised can also mean made all the same. «The high street has become homogenised, with the same chain shops in every town.» The clue is "the same", so homogenised means everything has become alike.
explain: Sometimes the word is used to criticise. «The film felt homogenised, with none of the surprises that made the book special.» The clue is "none of the surprises", so homogenised means dull, with the interesting differences taken away. Ask yourself: is the writer happy about it or not?
fact: Homogenise is the verb, and homogenised is its past form: to homogenise something is to make it all the same or mixed evenly.
fact: «Homogenised» milk has its fat droplets broken into tiny pieces, so the cream stays mixed in and does not rise to the top.
fact: When people call a place or a film «homogenised», they mean it has lost its interesting differences.
fact: In American spelling the word is homogenized, with a z, but the meaning is the same.
fact: A good check is to swap in «mixed evenly» or «all the same» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Homogenised milk stays smooth, and the cream does not rise to the top.» What does homogenised mean in this sentence? | Frozen solid | Sour and off | *Mixed evenly all the way through | Left to separate into layers
exercise: «Every town now has the same shops, so the high street feels homogenised.» What does homogenised mean here? | *Made all the same | Full of surprises and colour | Brand new and freshly painted
exercise: «The critic said the album sounded homogenised, with no surprises at all.» What does the critic mean? | The album is full of exciting surprises | The album is very loud | The album is in a foreign language | *The album sounds dull, with no interesting differences
test: «Yesterday the factory ___ the milk before bottling it.» Which word fits? | painted | sliced | frozen | *homogenised
test: «The museum wants to ___ its rooms so that every room looks exactly the same.» Which word fits? | shrink | rescue | *homogenise | brighten
exam: «Pupils said the new town centre felt homogenised, with the same shops in every street.» What does homogenised suggest about the town? | It is brand new and freshly painted | *It is dull and the same everywhere | It is in a different country | It is exciting and full of surprises
